  "text": "Grandma has finished The Empty Bench. Read it with help if you like, then let her share it with the people here.\n\nA little later, Rina lifted the golden loaves from the oven. She set them aside to cool, then chose one for Sol.\n\nDrag an object, then release to place it. Click a deck or the ground to walk. You can leave a repair unfinished.\n\nThe seed stays dark in a boat or a hand. Its lantern-flower grows only after its roots reach the garden’s soil.\n\nPip’s flower will show him planting the seed with Grandma. Place this picture in the lantern you grew together.\n\nRina says: “I promised to have everyone’s bread ready today. If those sacks get wet, I won’t be able to bake.”\n\nThe boy hesitates, then holds out his bird. He has accepted Mara’s help. Mara needs tape from the dock office.\n\nYou can listen to this recording during practice. The game removes it when you leave or start a new recording.\n\nPip watched Mara help passengers safely ashore. She stayed on duty because the last boat was still due later.\n\nClick a place to walk there, or use WASD and the arrow keys. Approach a person, then choose Talk or press E.\n\nA short time passes while the loaves bake. The gathering has not begun; Mara’s last boat is still due later.\n\nGrandma now understands why her friends stayed away. Her spare cushions are in the storage beside the bench.\n\nSol replaced the cracked roof tile. Water stopped entering through the opening while rain continued outside.\n\nMara wrote this story about an earlier visit. “I” means Mara; the boy speaks about his sister’s paper bird.\n\nMara says: “I’ll still be working. You can read my story for me. Please bring me one of Grandma’s stories.”\n\nMara says: “Thank you. I’ll read it after the last boat returns. It’s good to have a story from her again.”",
